@startuml trust-and-data-flow
!include _theme.iuml
left to right direction

package "Operator-controlled boundary" {
  file "Reviewed YAML policy" as Config
  file "Reviewed seed files" as Seeds
  rectangle "Environment secret\nGITHUB_TOKEN / GH_TOKEN" as Secret
  component "Octoform process" as Process
  rectangle "Console and CI log" as Output
}

cloud "Network trust boundary" as Network
package "GitHub-controlled boundary" {
  component "GitHub REST API" as API
  database "Repository and\norganization state" as State
}

Config --> Process : desired values and local paths
Seeds --> Process : content only when policy declares it
Secret --> Process : read into process memory
Process --> Network : authenticated HTTPS request
Network --> API : bearer credential in transit
API --> State : authorized read or mutation
State --> API : current state
API --> Network : response or error
Network --> Process : observed values and capability evidence
Process --> Output : findings, plan and outcomes

note top of Secret
  Use the minimum permissions needed.
  Store CI credentials as protected secrets.
  Rotate or revoke after suspected exposure.
end note

note bottom of Process
  0.3.1 reads tokens from the environment.
  It has no token field in configuration and
  no machine-readable plan artifact to persist.
end note

note bottom of Output
  Review logs before sharing them. GitHub errors
  and repository names can still be sensitive even
  when the credential itself is not printed.
end note
@enduml
